@startuml
title Add a task
actor User
participant MainActivity
participant TaskAdapter
participant TaskViewModel
participant TaskRepository
participant ExecutorService
participant TaskDao
participant Room
database SQLite
participant "LiveData<List<Task>>" as LiveData
note over MainActivity, LiveData
  In onCreate : getTasks().observe(this, observer).
  Repository retains the LiveData from TaskDao.observeAll().
  ViewModel exposes the same LiveData.
end note
User -> MainActivity : enter "Prepare the lab", click ADD
MainActivity -> MainActivity : trim / reject a blank title
MainActivity -> TaskViewModel : addTask(title)
TaskViewModel -> TaskViewModel : trim / validation / new Task(title)
TaskViewModel -> TaskRepository : insert(task)
TaskRepository -> ExecutorService : execute(lambda)
ExecutorService -> TaskDao : insert(task) [worker thread]
TaskDao -> Room : generated insert (@Insert)
Room -> SQLite : INSERT (transaction)
SQLite --> Room : id
Room --> TaskDao : id
TaskDao --> ExecutorService : long (unused)
Room -> Room : invalidates the observed table
Room -> SQLite : SELECT * FROM tasks ORDER BY id DESC
SQLite --> Room : updated rows
Room -> LiveData : publishes List<Task>
LiveData -> MainActivity : observer (UI thread, active Activity)
MainActivity -> TaskAdapter : submitList(tasks)
MainActivity -> MainActivity : updateCounter(tasks) / empty state
note over Room, MainActivity
  Room reruns the query in the background.
  SQLite never calls the Activity directly.
end note
@enduml
